<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><b>Relationship Between "Compensation actually paid" and Performance Measures</b></p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;text-indent:25pt;">The following illustrates and describes the relationship between the &#8220;compensation actually paid&#8221; to our named executive officers and the financial performance metrics disclosed in the pay versus performance table above. Below is the comparison of the "compensation actually paid" to our PEO and PFO to (a) Total Shareholder Return (TSR) and (b) Net Income (loss) for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024&#160;and 2025:</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;text-indent:25pt;">&#160;</p>

<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="finTable" style="width: 100%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; text-indent: 0px;">

